WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.130
If you want to hear about the secret murder
plot hidden within the world of Look-See,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:18.070
stick around to the end of this video.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:35.760
“If you yourself cannot release, then it
will come to take a piece…

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.690
But what does it mean release?

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.040
I’m not holding on to anything!

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:46.969
It couldn’t be talking releasing these 58
Things You Missed from CryptTV’s hit web-series

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:47.969
Look-See… could it?”

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:48.969
OK.

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:49.969
Alright fine.

00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:53.690
I was going to keep them to myself but here
they are.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.079
XX Things You Missed.

00:00:55.079 --> 00:00:58.260
Before we get started, you’ll definitely
want to have seen the CryptTV web-series Look-See,

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.890
so if you haven’t seen it yet, click or
tap right here to watch it before coming back

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:03.890
to this video.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:08.130
One of the things that’s never fully answered
in Look-See, is what the extent of the titular

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.760
creature’s supernatural powers actually
is.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.800
In other words, how is Look-See able to use
its abilities punish its victims?

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.690
Starting in episode one, it looks at first
glance that Look-See has the ability to teleport

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:21.970
or at least move extremely fast to catch people
who aren’t able to release.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:25.570
For example at the very beginning, this woman
runs into the bathroom as if she’s already

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:28.073
been chased, then checks all three stalls
to confirm that she’s alone.

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:32.700
She must do this because she already has an
idea of what Look-See is capable of and wants

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.610
to make sure she’s alone by checking every
inch of the bathroom she’s hiding out in.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:38.610
She eventually decides to hide in the middle
stall.

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:44.380
Now focus on this crack in the door.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.380
Did you catch that?

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.360
The creature crosses from left to right.

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:50.870
The only door in and out of the bathroom is
on the far right side.

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:52.800
So how did it get to the left side so quickly?

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.170
On top of that, The shoes end up appearing
under the stall back over on the left side.

00:01:57.170 --> 00:01:59.860
This constant movement puts the viewer on
edge.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:03.610
By breaking the rules of space, we’re never
sure where Look-See might appear.

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:07.150
There's another example of it’s uncanny
movement ability at the end when it appears

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:09.070
on the toilet seat behind her.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:12.340
In episode 2 it warps out of the Daniel’s
bedroom, then later warps in and out of the

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:15.530
shower area to kill the woman Daniel is having
an affair with.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.970
Then in episode 3 it shows up behind a bedroom
door.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.410
So how is it able to do this?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.940
Is it teleportation?

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.560
Episode 5 offers a couple possibilities to
solving this secret.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:26.980
First, we see the creature double itself.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:30.480
Daniel shows up at the hospital, but she soon
sees that he's also a victim of Look-See.

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.080
When he grabs her knee, pause it right there.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.710
It’s Look-See’s hand with Daniel’s arm.

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:39.050
I would infer that whenever we see someone
who has died come back to life, Look-See is

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:40.050
behind it.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:44.700
But Look-See also seems to possess the ability
to duplicate itself, because right here dead

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.770
Daniel and Look-See appear side by side.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:50.260
You can pause it to where they’re on screen
at the same time.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:54.800
There could be multiple copies of Look-See
helping create the illusion of teleportation.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.230
But that doesn’t explain how Look-See appears
in rooms that the characters have already

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.540
proven to be empty.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.500
Episode 5 may offer an answer for that as
well.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:07.010
The protagonist has an opportunity to attack
to Look-See, but despite having no eyes, it's

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:10.380
extremely fast reflexes and movement speed
help it get away.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.730
My theory is that Look-See has the ability
to move so fast, that if you let it out of

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:16.130
sight for a moment, it can rush to another
location.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.550
And it can do all of this quickly and quietly.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:21.430
That's not the only ability it has though.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:25.370
It's super flexible, enough to bend down so
it's head is down by its feet.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:28.670
It's strong enough to rip off body parts and
contort corpses.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.100
And it can open and close doors without touching
them.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.930
Honestly, it seems like it can do whatever
it wants, and tends to just toy with its victims.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:40.690
I wouldn't be surprised if we haven't seen
the full extent of what it's capable of yet.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:44.180
Despite all of this, it does seem fairly easy
to hurt Look-See.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.160
It gets injured when it's hand gets slammed
in the door in Episode 2 and when she stabs

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:50.340
it in the head in Episode 5.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.709
It doesn't stay down for long though, later
tossing the bloody fork back to mock her.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:03:58.230
Now that we've covered what the monster can
do, let's take a look at why.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.990
Each character receives the same note.

00:03:59.990 --> 00:04:04.099
“If you yourself cannot release, then it
will come to take a piece.”

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:05.830
Let's break it down down episode by episode.

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:09.560
The first woman won't release herself from
a marriage that has clearly gone south.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.510
If you've ever heard the term, “take her
hand in marriage”, you'll know why it's

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.730
symbolic that her hand was taken from her.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.540
And similarly, if you've ever heard the term,
“She walked out on her husband,” that

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.400
could be the reason her legs are broken.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.920
She is one of only two characters to survive
an encounter, so it's possible that Look-See

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.190
is actually giving her a second chance, so
that once her legs do heal, she'll appreciate

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.560
them enough to put them to good use, and walk
out on her man.

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:36.340
Another episode shows her writing tons of
notes for other victims, which makes me think

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:40.540
that there's kind of a Jigsaw-esque apprenticeship
going on here; like if you survive your game

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.090
you'll become a stronger person for it and
help setup the games for someone else.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:48.940
In fact, the themes in this series aren't
too dissimilar to those in the Saw franchise.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.840
In the next episode we see why she needs to
leave her marriage: because her husband is

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:54.210
seeing another woman.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:58.200
The adulterous woman wants more than to simply
sleep with Daniel though, she's got her eyes

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.190
set on being the replacement.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.950
She wants to be the girl whose face appears
next to him in that photo, which is why Look-See

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:05.310
takes away her head.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:08.460
She needed to release her idea of being with
a married man.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:12.310
There's evidence around the house that this
is the home of a man in a committed relationship.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.930
The obvious one if the picture on the bathroom
mirror, but she also steps outside briefly,

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:17.790
where you can see two heart shaped chairs.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:23.040
In the bathroom, a double shower head is installed,
one for the taller man and one for his wife.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.110
There's more backstory on why Daniel cheats
on his wife later in the series.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:28.680
But for now, let's move on to Episode 3.

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.910
The character in this one needs to release
his obsession with his deceased daughter who

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:33.310
drowned in an accident.

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:35.150
His release would be to move on with his life.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:39.660
We find him in a sad state, preparing his
daughter's would-be 13th birthday cake and

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:43.420
eating it by himself while flipping through
an album of old photos.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.870
This isn't just a one time thing for his daughter's
birthday.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:50.090
He still has cupboards locked up, something
you would do to prevent a child from getting

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:52.910
in, and seemingly he hasn't touched the daughter's
room.

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:57.320
He wants nothing more than to embrace his
child again, so Look-See removes his arms,

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:01.750
while leaving his hands and twists his head
around to signify that he needed to turn around

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.510
and stop looking to the past.

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.740
Episode 4 is where things really get interesting.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:08.870
It opens with the death of a high school student
at Harbor High.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:12.300
Shortly thereafter, we discover that there
are already 12 victims being investigated

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:14.139
and this kid is the 13th.

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:17.610
Pausing the video to read the small text uncovers
the reason for all the deaths.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.400
“Medication found poisoned.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.400
Laced over the counter.”

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.830
This is the biggest event that has happened
so far in the series.

00:06:23.830 --> 00:06:27.990
This headline confirms a mass murder plot,
and all signs point to it being someone other

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.290
than Look-See.

00:06:29.290 --> 00:06:32.360
There's even a possibility that it goes much
bigger than what is shown on screen.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:36.370
If medication was laced at a pharmacy, there
are probably other adult victims that we haven't

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.370
seen yet.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:40.080
This community has a mass murderer on its
hands.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.729
It's no wonder Look-See is drawn to this area,
because there must be countless people who

00:06:43.729 --> 00:06:58.080
need to release.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.540
This is actually where the whole saga begins.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.730
The series presents the episodes in an order
that lets us discover more about the monster

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.080
with each passing episode.

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.300
But CryptTV later released a special supercut
with the episodes arranged in chronological

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.300
order.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.470
It starts with this funeral episode, which
tells us a lot why there is so much grief

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:17.340
in this community; the reason that Look-See
comes here and pushes these people to release.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:22.000
It is here that we see the beginnings of Daniel
and his wife's relationship falling apart.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.600
I would assume they are at that funeral because
one of the 13 children who were poisoned was

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:29.940
theirs, and losing their child ours puts a
huge strain on their relationship.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:33.440
It's here that Daniel meets the woman who
he later has the affair with.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.790
Often in times of crisis it's comforting to
turn to someone you can relate to and unfortunately

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.490
in this case they develop a relationship.

00:07:40.490 --> 00:07:44.420
Daniel's wife finds out and that leads into
the next episode chronologically, where Look-See

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:46.539
forces her to release in the bathroom.

00:07:46.539 --> 00:07:50.870
Not long after, we have the infidelity episode,
and my theory is it's both Daniel and the

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.020
affair woman who are punished in this one.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.449
When she gets out of the bathroom, Daniel
is nowhere to be found because Look-See has

00:07:56.449 --> 00:08:01.100
already taken him, removing his eyes, because
it was his wandering eyes that initially led

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:02.800
him to check out this woman.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:07.110
And by the way, it may not have been the first
time his eyes were up to no good.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:11.060
Later that night, the wife wakes up in the
hospital and tries to kill Look-See, but she

00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.060
is unsuccessful.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:15.500
It's unclear how much time passes until the
final episode on the chronology, where Look-See

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:19.840
returns to punish the lingering father, at
the end of which Daniel's wife has become

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.539
Look-See’s note writing lackey.

00:08:21.539 --> 00:08:25.690
So if she's been the one writing the notes,
then who wrote her note on the bathroom stall

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.690
door?

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.500
That's also answered in episode 4.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:30.440
The short answer is: it’s this guy.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:32.990
But let’s take it back to the start of episode
4.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:37.619
The kid who dies in the opening shot, is featured
on the memorial, where we see this photo of

00:08:37.619 --> 00:08:38.619
him.

00:08:38.619 --> 00:08:39.619
I’m assuming that’s his sister.

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:40.619
Her name is Gretchen Holt.

00:08:40.619 --> 00:08:44.119
Turns out she’s a cop, and she’s tasked
with cleaning up the evidence markers.

00:08:44.119 --> 00:08:48.410
Her release is gonna involve moving on after
the tragedy, just like the guy from the 3rd

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.410
Episode.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:51.899
But in her case, she wants to do a little
bit of investigation on her own and starts

00:08:51.899 --> 00:08:55.550
to snoop around the school when something
out of the ordinary happens and she sees one

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:58.779
of kids who was covered in the sheets back
up and moving around.

00:08:58.779 --> 00:09:01.320
As we know, this is a manipulation of Look-See.

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:05.990
After coming face to f--... well, after an
encounter with Look-See, we finally meet the

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:12.129
mystery man, and he actually saves her, but
ends up getting picked off himself by creature.

00:09:12.129 --> 00:09:15.769
Gretchen actually survives, but the man is
forced to leave the message in the bathroom

00:09:15.769 --> 00:09:18.920
before eventually killing himself at the start
of episode 5.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:23.660
We don’t know a lot about this character,
so all I can do is theorize about what he

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.869
needed to release.

00:09:24.869 --> 00:09:28.519
His death may not be the best place to look
for clues like I did with the others, because

00:09:28.519 --> 00:09:32.619
it would appear that he committed suicide
to escape the torment of Look-See.

00:09:32.619 --> 00:09:34.440
So he got out on his own terms.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:39.120
All we know is that he was in the school at
night after the murders, sneaking around backstage.

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.660
You may not have noticed this in the background,
but when Holt surveys with her flashlight,

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:44.040
you can spot a girl facing the wall.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:48.569
My first inclination is that Mystery Man is
doing something to her when he notices Holt

00:09:48.569 --> 00:09:49.569
and kicks her out.

00:09:49.569 --> 00:09:53.510
He also makes a brief appearance at the funeral,
looking down on the crowd from above before

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:54.620
making his exit.

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:57.870
At this point, he’s looking like the top
suspect to be the murderer.

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:01.930
My guess is he has some kind of grudge against
society, and his release would be to simply

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:02.959
let it go.

00:10:02.959 --> 00:10:07.290
What he ends up doing instead, is killing
dozens of people, showing up the funeral to

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:10.970
watch the parents suffer, then returning to
the scene of the crime for some more foul

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:11.970
play.

00:10:11.970 --> 00:10:15.490
He knows Look-See is going do something horrible
to him, so he ends his life on his own terms

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:16.490
to get away.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.569
That’s the last death we see onscreen, because
the married woman ends up getting away at

00:10:20.569 --> 00:10:21.699
the end of episode 5.

00:10:21.699 --> 00:10:25.429
But that doesn’t mean the fifth episode
doesn’t still offer some clues about Look-See.

00:10:25.429 --> 00:10:28.480
There are some elements that keep popping
up for each victim.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:32.490
For example, the victims always seem to be
around flowers when Look-See attacks.

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:37.339
They can be seen beside the hospital bed,
the flower wallpaper in episode 3, also flowers

00:10:37.339 --> 00:10:42.809
on the cups, on the jars, on the toilet in
episode 2 and again on the wallpaper in episode

00:10:42.809 --> 00:10:43.809
1.

00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:47.269
The wallpaper design resembles the cracks
on the walls in episode 4 and the newspaper

00:10:47.269 --> 00:10:50.779
article in that episode encourages people
to bring flowers.

00:10:50.779 --> 00:10:54.779
Back in the first episode, a butterfly design
is seen on Look-See’s shoes, so Look-See

00:10:54.779 --> 00:10:59.679
could represent a butterfly going around from
flower to flower, or victim to victim, spreading

00:10:59.679 --> 00:11:00.679
its message.

00:11:00.679 --> 00:11:04.730
There are some other similarities, in the
attacks, but the meanings, if any, may not

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:05.740
be as clear.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:09.800
For example, I saw an apple and banana on
the scene of two of the attacks, and two of

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:12.079
them take place around 6 o’clock.

00:11:12.079 --> 00:11:16.029
That could have something to do with the stopwatch,
which comes in the shape of an eye, the one

00:11:16.029 --> 00:11:18.560
feature that Look-See noticeably does not
have.

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:22.600
The stop watch could be a countdown for how
long someone has to “release” before they

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:25.139
are punished, but those details are yet to
be seen.

00:11:25.139 --> 00:11:28.319
One conclusion I would like to make however,
is that the body parts that Look-See collects

00:11:28.319 --> 00:11:31.389
from people make up Look-See.

00:11:31.389 --> 00:11:34.889
Looking at its design, Look-See does seem
to be stitched together from a bunch of various

00:11:34.889 --> 00:11:39.790
body parts, and we see the main character’s
own hand used to give her the stopwatch near

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:40.790
the end.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:45.579
As I mentioned, Look-See is prominently lacking
eyes considering it’s name is a portmaneau

00:11:45.579 --> 00:11:50.279
of the words look and see, the two verbs most
commonly associated with eyes.

00:11:50.279 --> 00:11:54.089
It will be interesting to see what Look-See
ends up doing with Daniel’s eyes.

00:11:54.089 --> 00:11:58.589
That brings me to my last Thing You Missed,
which is this title card asking about what

00:11:58.589 --> 00:11:59.589
will happen next.

00:11:59.589 --> 00:12:03.410
That may be the end of season 1, but it appears
that there are plans to bring Look-See back

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.059
for a second season.

00:12:05.059 --> 00:12:08.739
You don’t want to miss out what happens
next, so I’ll leave you this link to subscribe

00:12:08.739 --> 00:12:12.740
to CryptTV to stay up to date on Look-See
and plenty of other great short horror content.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.589
Let me know some of your own theories about
Look-See and where you think the series will

00:12:16.589 --> 00:12:18.120
go from here in the comments.

00:12:18.120 --> 00:12:20.139
I will see you in the next one.

00:12:20.139 --> 00:12:21.220
Assuming we both survive.

